# ─── STANDALONE DEMO BUILD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loaded automatically by `vite build --mode demo` (npm run build:demo), which
# produces the bundle served at https://incontrol.ctrlplusf.com.
#
# This file IS committed on purpose: it holds no secret. The "password" below is
# compiled into the JavaScript sent to every visitor and is a doorbell, not a lock
# (see the header of src/lib/demoGate.ts). Everything behind it is fictitious.
#
# ⚠️ NEVER add VITE_DEMO_STANDALONE to the Vercel project. It is the one switch
# that lets a production build run on demo data — in Vercel that would point the
# real system at fictitious rows. See docs/08-DEMO-DEPLOYMENT.md.

VITE_DEMO_STANDALONE=true

# ── One password per product tier ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The password you hand a prospect IS the tier they see. There is deliberately no
# tier picker in the UI: someone who can choose will always choose the top one,
# which defeats the point of showing each person the level that fits them.
#
# The tiers themselves are defined in src/lib/tiers.ts — moving a feature between
# levels is an edit there, not here.
#
# ⚠️ These three share a visible pattern. That is fine for a marketing demo (the
# worst case is a prospect seeing MORE than intended, which is an upsell), but if
# you ever need the levels genuinely sealed off, replace them with three unrelated
# strings. They are not secrets either way — see src/lib/demoGate.ts.
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD_BASIC=INCONTROL-BASIC
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD_ADVANCED=INCONTROL-PRO
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD=INCONTROL2026

# ── Branding for this build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The demo is the PRODUCT being shown, not the client running it, so it carries
# its own name. Only these four strings are overridable (src/brand.config.ts);
# the palette stays shared, so the demo always looks like the real system.
#
# VITE_BRAND_GREETING is deliberately NOT the system name: the dashboard greets
# the person sitting in front of it, and in a public demo that person is a guest.
VITE_BRAND_NAME=incontrol
VITE_BRAND_TAB_TITLE=incontrol
VITE_BRAND_GREETING=אורח

# The default logo must NOT be the client's. /logo.png is the Hadas wordmark — it
# literally has "Hadas" written in it — so the demo ships its own mark instead.
# Replace both with a real incontrol logo whenever there is one; nothing else
# needs to change. (Inside the running demo, Settings → העדפות can also swap the
# logo for the length of a session.)
VITE_BRAND_LOGO=/incontrol-logo.svg
VITE_BRAND_FAVICON=/incontrol-logo.svg

# Not used — in demo mode the Supabase client is fully stubbed and never dials out.
# They are set to syntactically valid junk because src/lib/supabase.ts constructs the
# client at module level, and supabase-js throws on an empty URL, which would render
# a blank page instead of an error anyone could read.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://demo.invalid
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=demo-mode-no-key-needed
